# Line endings, settled once, for everyone.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (P15.S12). This repo is developed on Windows with
# `core.autocrlf=true` and built in CI on ubuntu-latest. Without a
# `.gitattributes` the working tree's line endings depend on each clone's local
# git config, which is a property of the machine rather than of the project --
# so two developers can read the same committed bytes as different strings.
#
# That is not theoretical here. P15.S5 lost real time to it twice in one step:
# a test asserted against a literal "\n" and failed on a Windows checkout that
# had CRLF, and its sibling was worse and did NOT fail -- an `indexOf` returned
# -1, `slice(0, -1)` handed it nearly the whole file as the "rule body", and the
# assertions passed against the wrong string. A test that passes for the wrong
# reason is more expensive than one that fails.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: git decides what is text, normalises it to LF in the
# repository, and checks it out as LF. Committed bytes stop depending on who
# committed them. CI and production already saw LF; this makes the working tree
# agree.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must keep CRLF to work on Windows, regardless of the rule above.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts and git hooks must be LF or they will not execute on Linux --
# `#!/usr/bin/env sh\r` is not a program name.
*.sh    text eol=lf
.husky/* text eol=lf

# BINARY. Declared explicitly rather than left to git's heuristic, because the
# cost of a wrong guess is silent corruption, not a diff. The PNGs in
# particular are the Playwright visual baselines: a single byte of EOL
# translation in one of those turns all nine landing regression tests red with
# no cause visible in the diff.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.TTF   binary
*.otf   binary
*.OTF   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary

# Lockfiles are generated: collapse them in diffs and never merge them by hand.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated

# Keep the prototype out of language stats; CLAUDE.md §13 says it is
# reference-only and is never migrated.
legacy/** linguist-vendored
